 other x86 processors, is now used expansively by 98% of the top 1,000 EC2 customers. The same story arc is unfolding in AI. Our second version of our custom AI silicon (Trainium2) had about 30% better price-performance than comparable GPUs, and has largely sold out. Trainium3, which just started shipping at the start of 2026 and is 30-40% more price-performant than Trainium2, is nearly fully-subscribed. A significant chun"},{"end_char":8000,"id":"view-f6e228b6d411-7000","start_char":7000,"text":"k of Trainium4, which is still about 18 months from broad availability, has already been reserved. And, Amazon Bedrock, AWS’s primary (and very fast-growing) inference service, runs most of its inference on Trainium. Demand for Trainium is booming.\\nHaving our own hotly demanded AI chip opens up many possibilities, but perhaps none larger than the ability to lower costs for customers and secure better economics for AWS. At scale, we expect Trainium will save us tens of billions of capex dollars per year, and provide several hundred basis points of operating margin advantage versus relying on others’ chips for inference.  \\nOur annual revenue run rate for our chips business (inclusive of Graviton, Trainium, and Nitro—our EC2 NIC) is now over $20 billion, and growing triple digit percentages YoY. To dimensionalize this versus other chips companies, that run rate is somewhat understated by our currently only monetizing our chips through EC2. If our chips business was a stand-alone busines"}],"selected_text_chars":8000,"selection_vocabulary":["revenue","capex","capital","capacity","paid","utilization","rent","h100","energy","electricity","data center","trainium","graviton","nitro","quarter","billion","million"],"source_text_field":"canonical_payload_json","view_version":"fixed-metric-vocabulary-1000char-windows-v1"}}],"proposed_decision":{"action":"stop","action_id":null,"answer":"Amazon reported that its chips business—spanning Trainium, Graviton, and Nitro—exceeded a $20 billion annual revenue run rate (reported in Q1 2026) and subsequently exceeded a $25 billion annual revenue run rate (reported around Q2 2026). The figure does not isolate AI-only revenue, as it explicitly includes Graviton (CPUs for general cloud computing) and the Nitro System (networking, storage, and security / EC2 NIC).","expected_result":"","rationale":"The visible evidence from Amazon's reported releases specifies the annual revenue run rate for the chips business inclusive of Graviton, Trainium, and Nitro. In Q1 2026 it exceeded $20 billion, and as reported in Q2 2026 / the history article, it exceeded a $25 billion annual revenue run rate. The evidence also explicitly states that this figure includes Graviton (general cloud computing CPUs) and Nitro (EC2 NIC/networking, storage, security), meaning it does not isolate AI-only revenue.","stop_reason":"question answered","uncertainty":""},"question":"What annual run rate does the saved primary source report for the combined Trainium, Graviton and Nitro business, and does that figure isolate AI-only revenue?"}

